{
  "title": "64: al-Taghaabon التغابن",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيُسَبِّحُ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِۚ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(1)\nYOSABBEHO LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE LAHUL A’LAYNAA LAHUL HAMDO WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nHalloweth the Glory of God whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; His (exclusively) is the Kingdom and unto Him (only) is due (all) praise, and He (alone) is over all things All-Powerful.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ فَمِنْكُمْ كَافِرٌ وَّمِنْكُمْ مُّؤْمِنٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(2)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM FA MINKUM KAAFERUN WWAMENKUM MMUMENUN WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nHe it is Who created you, then some of you are disbelievers and (some) of you are believers; and God seest all whatsoever ye do.\nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَوَّرَكُمْ فَاَحْسَنَ صُوَرَكُمْۚ وَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(3)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE WASAWRAKUM FA AHSANAL SOORAKUM WA ELAYHE MASEER.\nCreated He the heavens and the earth with Truth and fashioned you and made good your forms and unto Him (only) is the ultimate resort.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُوْنَؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(4)\nYA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YA’LAMO MAA TUSERROONA WA MAA TUA’LENOONA WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nKnoweth He whatsoever is in the heavens and the earth and knoweth He whatsoever ye conceal and whatsoever ye declare; and God knoweth all of whatsoever is in the breasts (hearts).\nاَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ نَبَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ فَذَاقُوْا وَبَالَ اَمْرِهِمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(5)\nALAM YAATEKUM NABAUA LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QABLO FA ZAAQOO WA BAALA AMREHIM WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nHath not come unto you the story of those who disbelieved before, then tasted they the evil consequences of their (own) doings; and for them shall be a painful chastisement.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهٗ كَانَتْ تَّاْتِيْهِمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَقَالُوْۤا اَبَشَرٌ يَّهْدُوْنَنَا فَكَفَرُوْا وَتَوَلَّوْا وَّاسْتَغْنَى اللّٰهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَنِىٌّ حَمِيْدٌ‏(6)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHU KAANAT TTAATEEHEM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FA-QAALOO AABASHARUN YYAHDOONANAA FA KAFAROO WA TAWALLAW WWAASTAGHNAA LAAHO WAL LAAHO GHANIYYUN HAMEED.\nThat because there had come their apostles with clear proofs, but said they: “What! shall men (mortals like unto us) guide us?” So disbelieved they and they turned away, and God needeth not (anything), and God is Self Sufficient, The Most Praised.\nزَعَمَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنْ لَّنْ يُّبْعَثُوْا ؕ قُلْ بَلٰى وَرَبِّىْ لَتُبْعَثُنَّ ثُمَّ لَتُنَبَّؤُنَّ بِمَا عَمِلْتُمْؕ وَذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(7)\nZAA’AMA LAZEENA KAFAROO AN LAN-Y YYUBA’ASOOA QUL BALAA WA RABBEE LATUBA’ASUNNA SUMMA LATUNABBAUNNA BEMAA A’AMELTUM WAZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERUN.\nThink those who disbelieve that never shall they be raised. Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!’)’. “Aye! By my Lord! certainly shall ye be raised, then certainly shall ye be informed of what ye did; and that, for God, is easy.\nفَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَالنُّوْرِ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلْنَاؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(8)\nFA AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA NOORE LAZEE AANZALNAA WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nSo believe ye in God and His Apostle and the Light We have sent down; and God is Well-Aware of whatsoever ye do.\nيَوْمَ يَجْمَعُكُمْ لِيَوْمِ الْجَمْعِ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ التَّغَابُنِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّؤْمِنْۢ بِاللّٰهِ وَيَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا يُّكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَيِّاٰتِهٖ وَيُدْخِلْهُ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِیْمُ‏(9)\nYAWMA YAJMAU’UKUM LE-YAWMIL AL-JAME’E ZAA LEKA YAWMUD AT-TAGHAABUNE WA MAN YOAMIM BIL-LAAHE WA YA’MAL SAALEHAN YYUKAFFER A’NHO WA WA YUDKHILHO JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM ZAA LEKA FAWZUL AL-A’AZEMU.\nThe day that He will gather you for the day of gathering, that is the day of mutual loss; and whosoever believeth in God and doeth good, He will wipe out from him his sins and admit him into gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, to abide therein for ever; that is a great achievement.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(10)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nAnd those who disbelieved and belied Our signs, they are the fellows of the fire, to abide therein; and wretched is the destination.\nمَاۤ اَصَابَ مِنْ مُّصِيْبَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَنْ يُّؤْمِنْۢ بِاللّٰهِ يَهْدِ قَلْبَهٗؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(11)\nMAA ASAABA MIN MMUSEEBATIN ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WA MAN YOAMIM BIL-LAAHE YAHDE QALBAH WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAfflicteth not any affliction save by the leave of God; and whosoever believeth in God, He guideth aright his heart; and verily God well-knoweth all things.\nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَۚ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاِنَّمَا عَلٰى رَسُوْلِنَا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(12)\nWAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R FA-IN TAWALLAYTUM FA-INNAMAA A’LAA RASOOLENAA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd obey ye God, and obey ye the Apostle! And if ye turn away, then upon Our Apostle is only the clear delivery (of Our Message).\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(13)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nGod, there is no god but He; and upon God (alone) should rely the believers.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ مِنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ وَاَوْلَادِكُمْ عَدُوًّا لَّكُمْ فَاحْذَرُوْهُمْۚ وَاِنْ تَعْفُوْا وَتَصْفَحُوْا وَتَغْفِرُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(14)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL MIN AAZWAAJEKUM WAAWLAADEKUM A’DUWWAL LAKUM FAAHZAROOHUM WA TAA’FOOA WATASFAHOOA WATAGHFEROOA FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! Verily of your wives and your children (some are) enemy unto you; wherefore beware of them, and if ye forgive, overlook and cover up (their ills) then verily God is Oft-Forgiving, The Most Merciful.\nاِنَّمَاۤ اَمْوَالُكُمْ وَاَوْلَادُكُمْ فِتْنَةٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(15)\nINNAMAA AMWAALOKUM WA LAA AWLAADOKUM FITNATUN WAL LAAHO I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nVerily your possessions and your children are only a trial and verily God it is (He) with Whom is a great recompense.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ وَاسْمَعُوْا وَاَطِيْعُوْا وَاَنْفِقُوْا خَيْرًا لِّاَنْفُسِكُمْؕ وَمَنْ يُّوْقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهٖ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(16)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA MAA ENIS TA-TA’TUM WAS MA-O’O WAATEEU’OOA WA ANFEQOO KHAYRAN LEAANFUSEKUM WA MAN YOOQA SHOH-HA WA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nSo fear ye (the wrath of) God as much as ye can, and listen ye (unto His word), obey ye (only Him), and spend ye (in His way), it is better for yourselves; and whosoever is saved from the greed of his (own) self, these it is who are the successful ones.\nاِنْ تُقْرِضُوا اللّٰهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا يُّضٰعِفْهُ لَكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ شَكُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌۙ‏(17)\nIN TUQREZOOA LAAHA QARZAN HASANAN YYUZAAE’EFHU LAKUM WA YAGHFIR LAKUM WAL LAAHO SHAKOORUN HALEEM.\nIf ye lend God a goodly loan, He will double it unto you and will forgive you; And God is Most Appreciating, the Most Forbearing.\nعٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(18)\nA’ALEMUL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nThe Knower of (all things) the unseen and the seen, the Ever-Prevalent, the All-Wise.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Taghaabon (The Loss And Gain)\nThis Surah has 18 verses and it was revealed in Madinah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites this Surah will be safe at the time of his death.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person recites this Surah in the faraa’idh (compulsory prayers) then on the Day of Judgement this Surah itself will intercede on his behalf until he is allowed to enter Jannah. It is also narrated that one who recites this Surah will be protected from the tyranny of the rulers."
}
